1
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:11,867
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:32,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,367
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:41,067
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,967
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,233
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:46,467
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,167 --> 00:00:51,300
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:53,333
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:55,400
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,633 --> 00:00:58,133
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:00,367
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,267
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:06,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:09,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:11,767
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:12,967
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:22,400
<i>I'm accepting my suspension
because I deserve it.</i>

21
00:01:22,533 --> 00:01:24,900
<i>I just have a few suggestions
for the people we've arrested.</i>

22
00:01:25,033 --> 00:01:28,500
<i>Why don't we put Mr. Chan
and Tiger in the same cell?</i>

23
00:01:28,633 --> 00:01:30,833
<i>They're aggressive spiders
trapped in a box.</i>

24
00:01:30,967 --> 00:01:33,300
<i>What, one small reporter
beat you all up?</i>

25
00:01:33,433 --> 00:01:34,833
<i>It's not the reporter
who beat us up.</i>

26
00:01:34,967 --> 00:01:37,633
<i>If you've just followed
what I told you,</i>

27
00:01:37,767 --> 00:01:39,033
<i> they wouldn't have failed!</i>

28
00:01:39,167 --> 00:01:40,267
<i> I'll make him pay!</i>

29
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,433
<i>I'm going to file
a police report.</i>

30
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:43,000
<i> Sir, this way. Follow me.</i>

31
00:01:43,133 --> 00:01:45,500
<i>Damn it.
He got terribly lucky.</i>

32
00:01:45,633 --> 00:01:47,367
<i>Look at what your son did
to the motorcycle.</i>

33
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,633
<i>I saved someone, that's why
the motorcycle got ruined.</i>

34
00:01:49,767 --> 00:01:53,633
<i>The man I saved gave me money.
Here. It's for--</i>

35
00:01:54,433 --> 00:01:55,433
<i>Come on, son.
Take it. It's yours.</i>

36
00:01:55,567 --> 00:01:57,433
<i>This is not a good day
for Sam.</i>

37
00:01:57,567 --> 00:01:58,667
<i>- Let's go for some drinks!
- Yes?</i>

38
00:01:58,800 --> 00:01:59,700
<i>- Yes?
- Yes?</i>

39
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:01,400
<i> It's a yes!</i>

40
00:02:01,533 --> 00:02:04,067
<i>Treat your friends.
They helped you big time.</i>

41
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:09,167
- Salvador!
- Sir.

42
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:12,500
Looks like you still come
to us when you have a problem.

43
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:16,067
Well, you're involved in this!

44
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:20,567
You want to get revenge
because of my reports.

45
00:02:21,267 --> 00:02:22,933
Watch your mouth.

46
00:02:25,133 --> 00:02:26,967
Who even are you
for us to retaliate?

47
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,067
Admit it or not...

48
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,933
Who wants me beat up?
Who wants me killed?

49
00:02:32,567 --> 00:02:34,567
Was it your men?

50
00:02:35,167 --> 00:02:38,133
You keep making accusations
when you have no evidence.

51
00:02:38,267 --> 00:02:40,700
There is no such thing
as police brutality.

52
00:02:40,833 --> 00:02:43,600
But there is reporter brutality.

53
00:02:43,733 --> 00:02:47,567
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!
Calm down! Calm down!

54
00:02:50,133 --> 00:02:51,100
[ESTRELLA] Ma'am.

55
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:56,100
The reporter's here. Salvador.

56
00:02:56,233 --> 00:02:58,400
- He's beaten up!
- Why?

57
00:02:58,533 --> 00:03:00,400
He's here to file
a police report.

58
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:02,800
Come on. Let's go.

59
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:04,700
[SALVADOR] You want evidence?

60
00:03:04,833 --> 00:03:05,767
[JACKET THUDS]

61
00:03:07,867 --> 00:03:09,533
Fine, here! Watch this!

62
00:03:09,667 --> 00:03:11,700
[BLOWS LANDING OVER PHONE]

63
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,633
Well? Well?

64
00:03:14,333 --> 00:03:17,100
Surprised?
Your faces look guilty.

65
00:03:17,233 --> 00:03:19,333
Or maybe your boss is
involved in this, too,

66
00:03:19,467 --> 00:03:21,967
that General Jacinto!

67
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:23,167
That's just a video!

68
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:25,900
You still have no proof
we ordered that.

69
00:03:26,033 --> 00:03:28,167
You've got to be careful
with your words, you know?

70
00:03:28,300 --> 00:03:30,133
We can sue you for slander!

71
00:03:30,267 --> 00:03:31,733
That's what you do best!

72
00:03:31,867 --> 00:03:34,667
You keep scaring those
who go against you, right?

73
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,933
Luckily, a man saved me.

74
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:38,867
[SCOFFS]

75
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:42,367
Sir Salvador!

76
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:46,467
Are you here to ask us
to help you?

77
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:49,967
Or are you trying to prove
that you are our enemy?

78
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,933
[JACKET FLUTTERS]

79
00:03:55,467 --> 00:03:58,167
Hey! Jacinto, huh?

80
00:03:58,867 --> 00:04:01,233
What's your relation to that
heartless General Jacinto?

81
00:04:02,267 --> 00:04:03,367
General Jacinto...

82
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:05,567
...is my father.

83
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:08,367
Well, that's it!
You know the answer!

84
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,833
Why ask me?

85
00:04:09,967 --> 00:04:12,000
You should know the answer
if you have this.

86
00:04:12,133 --> 00:04:13,533
A brain!

87
00:04:13,667 --> 00:04:15,900
I can tolerate you
raising your voice.

88
00:04:16,767 --> 00:04:19,033
But never slander my father.

89
00:04:19,167 --> 00:04:21,400
What? You all planned
to have me killed?

90
00:04:22,033 --> 00:04:24,633
The truth will come out!
I won't leave you alone.

91
00:04:24,767 --> 00:04:27,133
I'll get my revenge.
I'll get my revenge!

92
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:30,100
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

93
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:36,067
[MAX] Sir.

94
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:39,167
What was Salvador saying?
Someone wants him dead?

95
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:42,267
Don't believe
that reporter's words.

96
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:44,167
All he says is fake news!

97
00:04:44,933 --> 00:04:47,033
Sir, please
let me handle this case.

98
00:04:47,167 --> 00:04:50,333
I'll prove to him that
what he's saying is wrong.

99
00:04:50,467 --> 00:04:52,067
This is not even journalism.

100
00:04:52,567 --> 00:04:53,667
It's fiction!

101
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,967
No, Lieutenant Jacinto.

102
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:57,367
It's pointless.

103
00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:00,467
The report will just be biased
because of your last name.

104
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,233
Sir.

105
00:05:02,367 --> 00:05:05,033
Shouldn't we check what the
people are complaining about?

106
00:05:05,933 --> 00:05:08,600
Of course, we'll investigate.

107
00:05:09,433 --> 00:05:11,933
Umali, Santos,
you handle the case.

108
00:05:12,667 --> 00:05:13,900
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

109
00:05:14,033 --> 00:05:21,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

110
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,833
- [UMALI] Sir.
- What the hell?!

111
00:05:30,133 --> 00:05:31,900
Is what I'm asking you
to do difficult?

112
00:05:32,033 --> 00:05:33,900
- Was it that hard?!
- Hold on, sir!

113
00:05:34,067 --> 00:05:35,967
- Sir, please!
- Don't touch me!

114
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,533
I just found out about it too.

115
00:05:37,667 --> 00:05:39,133
It's just Salvador.

116
00:05:39,267 --> 00:05:40,967
A low-rate reporter.

117
00:05:41,100 --> 00:05:43,833
Now he has evidence against us!

118
00:05:44,333 --> 00:05:47,367
Sir, don't worry.
I'll talk to Paquito.

119
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:50,800
I'll go back to Ginintuang Lupa
and find out what happened.

120
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:54,633
Find out what happened.

121
00:05:54,767 --> 00:05:57,233
- Am I clear?
- Yes, sir.

122
00:05:57,367 --> 00:05:58,567
But, sir...

123
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:01,233
Will we say that we're the ones
who had Salvador beaten up?

124
00:06:01,733 --> 00:06:04,267
We're the ones who asked
Salvador to be beaten up, right?

125
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,100
Use your brain!

126
00:06:06,433 --> 00:06:08,867
Whoever saved Salvador

127
00:06:09,033 --> 00:06:12,333
is the reason why we're
in trouble right now!

128
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:15,133
Find out who he is.

129
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:17,000
Okay?

130
00:06:17,133 --> 00:06:18,533
Alright, sir.

131
00:06:18,667 --> 00:06:21,467
I'm just making it clear,
so I understand, sir.

132
00:06:22,367 --> 00:06:24,000
You little--

133
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:28,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

134
00:06:30,067 --> 00:06:32,067
[BOKBOK] I'm hungry, Kulot.

135
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:35,000
Aren't we going
to cash these out yet?

136
00:06:35,133 --> 00:06:37,600
This stuff we gathered
still isn't enough.

137
00:06:37,733 --> 00:06:42,033
We need more
so we can buy food.

138
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:44,267
I'm really hungry, Curly.

139
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,200
I haven't eaten since yesterday.

140
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,533
[BINOY] Where will
you treat us, Gabi?

141
00:06:48,667 --> 00:06:50,267
- [GABO CHUCKLES]
- [TOLITS] Somewhere fancy!

142
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:53,200
I should've changed
into a killer outfit!

143
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:54,533
- [BONG] Oh no...
- [LAUGHTER]

144
00:06:54,667 --> 00:06:55,867
Killer outfit? More like
an outfit for the dead.

145
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,033
[LAUGHTER]

146
00:06:57,167 --> 00:06:59,600
I know you all,
you're all big eaters!

147
00:06:59,733 --> 00:07:01,533
- Especially you!
- [LAUGHTER]

148
00:07:01,667 --> 00:07:03,933
I know that Gabo
said that he'll treat us,

149
00:07:04,067 --> 00:07:07,133
but don't abuse it.
He still has bills to pay.

150
00:07:07,267 --> 00:07:09,433
[IPE] Let's just be grateful
that Gabo is treating us.

151
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,867
Hey, Curly, look!
Look!

152
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,133
Let's go!

153
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:21,300
[TENSE PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:07:28,133 --> 00:07:30,567
- [WOMAN] Hey!
- [CHILD] She's coming!

155
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:33,300
[WOMAN] Stop that!
Hey, you thieves!

156
00:07:33,667 --> 00:07:35,233
- Give those back!
- [CHILDREN LAUGHS]

157
00:07:35,367 --> 00:07:37,967
Come back here, you thieves!

158
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:43,833
[CHILDREN SHOUTING]

159
00:07:43,967 --> 00:07:45,967
[WOMAN] Come back here,
you thieves!

160
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,767
Help me!
Those kids stole my goods!

161
00:07:48,933 --> 00:07:50,100
These kids!

162
00:07:50,233 --> 00:07:51,833
[WOMAN] You shameless kids!

163
00:07:51,967 --> 00:07:54,600
[CHILDREN SHOUTING]

164
00:07:54,733 --> 00:07:56,033
[WOMAN] Stop them!

165
00:07:57,867 --> 00:07:59,367
Where the hell
are your parents?!

166
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:01,267
- [CHILDREN CRYING]
- [LOUD SLAP]

167
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,800
That's enough, please!

168
00:08:02,933 --> 00:08:05,567
- [CHILDREN CRYING]
- [WOMAN] You thieves!

169
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:06,833
[LOUD SLAP]

170
00:08:06,967 --> 00:08:09,300
[CHILDREN CRYING]

171
00:08:09,433 --> 00:08:10,600
Stop!

172
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,233
What's going on?!

173
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:15,167
[WOMAN] Gabo,
mind your own business.

174
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,333
Those kids stole from me!

175
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:28,667
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

176
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:31,833
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

177
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:33,200
How much was it?

178
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:34,600
I'll pay for it.

179
00:08:34,733 --> 00:08:36,600
200 pesos! Give it to me now!

180
00:08:36,733 --> 00:08:39,433
[TEKLA] I don't think
it's that much. She's bluffing.

181
00:08:41,933 --> 00:08:43,200
Here.

182
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:44,800
I'm sorry.

183
00:08:44,933 --> 00:08:49,000
The next time those kids
try to steal from me again,

184
00:08:49,133 --> 00:08:50,900
they'll get a good beating!

185
00:08:51,033 --> 00:08:52,067
I'm really sorry.

186
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,967
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]
- [BINOY] What a cranky lady.

187
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,633
Are you okay?

188
00:08:57,767 --> 00:08:59,133
You kids alright?

189
00:08:59,267 --> 00:09:00,333
I'm fine.

190
00:09:02,467 --> 00:09:03,867
[TEKLA] You kids are going
to get an earful.

191
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,067
Come here.

192
00:09:07,467 --> 00:09:08,533
Why did you do that?

193
00:09:09,733 --> 00:09:11,133
Why did you steal food?

194
00:09:11,267 --> 00:09:15,133
Gabo, we haven't eaten anything.

195
00:09:15,267 --> 00:09:19,367
Our parents
haven't given us food.

196
00:09:20,167 --> 00:09:21,833
But you shouldn't steal.

197
00:09:21,967 --> 00:09:23,367
You know it's bad.

198
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:27,367
We didn't want to steal these.

199
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:30,500
But we haven't eaten
since last night.

200
00:09:30,667 --> 00:09:32,567
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:33,900
- Fine.
- [KID SNIFFLES]

202
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:37,167
But you have to promise
not to do it again.

203
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:39,667
- Yes, Gabo!
- Yes, Gabo!

204
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Here.

205
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,267
I'm giving you money.

206
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,667
Buy something to eat.

207
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,900
If there's any left,
bring it home.

208
00:09:53,033 --> 00:09:56,167
If you need something
or you're hungry, just find me.

209
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:57,967
Okay?

210
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:00,167
- Yes, Gabo!
- Yes, Gabo!

211
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,367
Here. Go home.

212
00:10:02,533 --> 00:10:04,900
- Come on, hurry!
- Get going, kids. Go home.

213
00:10:06,733 --> 00:10:07,833
Gabo,

214
00:10:07,967 --> 00:10:09,833
you're a completely
different man.

215
00:10:09,967 --> 00:10:11,533
You've changed so much.

216
00:10:11,667 --> 00:10:13,633
You were just like
those kids before,

217
00:10:13,767 --> 00:10:15,100
running around with Django.

218
00:10:16,067 --> 00:10:18,100
I learned a lot from prison.

219
00:10:19,333 --> 00:10:21,300
I know how hard life inside was.

220
00:10:22,567 --> 00:10:23,933
I don't want those kids

221
00:10:25,033 --> 00:10:26,900
to do the same bad things
I've done.

222
00:10:27,033 --> 00:10:28,900
Exactly! Gabo's right.

223
00:10:29,033 --> 00:10:32,500
We shouldn't be tolerating
the kids' wrongdoings.

224
00:10:32,633 --> 00:10:34,233
We're the adults.

225
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,867
We should be teaching them
good manners

226
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,733
and right conduct, am I right?

227
00:10:40,867 --> 00:10:42,267
- Let's go.
- It's time for a drink.

228
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,033
- [CHEERING]
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:10:44,167 --> 00:10:46,467
That 500 pesos
was supposed to be for drinks.

230
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,633
Let it go!
Those are for the kids!

231
00:10:48,767 --> 00:10:50,033
You're so selfish.

232
00:10:50,167 --> 00:10:52,333
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

233
00:11:00,067 --> 00:11:01,433
[KNOB CLICKS, DOOR OPENS]

234
00:11:03,667 --> 00:11:05,333
- Oli.
- Salvador.

235
00:11:05,467 --> 00:11:07,000
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:08,033
[JACKET THUDS]

237
00:11:08,867 --> 00:11:10,467
Hey, hey, man!

238
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,533
What's that on your face?
What happened to you?

239
00:11:12,667 --> 00:11:13,767
What do you think?

240
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:14,933
I went to the salon.

241
00:11:15,067 --> 00:11:16,367
I had a makeover.

242
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:17,967
I got beaten up.

243
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,233
Oh god.

244
00:11:20,367 --> 00:11:22,067
[TAPS DOOR] Salvador!

245
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:23,133
What took you so long?

246
00:11:23,267 --> 00:11:24,833
We've been waiting for hours!

247
00:11:24,967 --> 00:11:26,333
It's only the first day
of taping,

248
00:11:26,467 --> 00:11:28,133
and you're already
acting like a diva.

249
00:11:28,267 --> 00:11:30,367
Boss, boss. Look, look.

250
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:32,533
He got beaten up.
He got in trouble.

251
00:11:33,567 --> 00:11:35,233
- Who did to you?
- [OLI CLEARS THROAT]

252
00:11:35,367 --> 00:11:38,033
A group of criminals.

253
00:11:38,167 --> 00:11:40,167
They ganged up and attacked me.

254
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:43,633
Luckily, a man helped me.

255
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,600
It's our pilot episode today!

256
00:11:45,733 --> 00:11:48,467
You can't be on camera
looking like that!

257
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:49,667
Didn't you hear me, boss?

258
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:51,067
I was assaulted!

259
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:53,267
I almost got killed.

260
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:56,800
All because of the news
you asked me to report.

261
00:11:56,933 --> 00:11:57,967
That's it.

262
00:11:58,667 --> 00:12:00,133
That's the grit I want.

263
00:12:00,267 --> 00:12:01,700
Courageous.

264
00:12:01,833 --> 00:12:03,600
That's what the country needs.

265
00:12:03,733 --> 00:12:06,000
That's what
the masses want, Salvador.

266
00:12:06,133 --> 00:12:07,200
Exactly that!

267
00:12:07,933 --> 00:12:10,600
You're so freaking cute!

268
00:12:11,733 --> 00:12:12,700
Perfect!

269
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:13,900
Do exactly like that!

270
00:12:14,033 --> 00:12:16,500
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

271
00:12:16,667 --> 00:12:18,233
- [DOOR CLOSES]
- [CLEARS THROAT]

272
00:12:18,367 --> 00:12:21,467
Deborah and I are going
to the NCIA office.

273
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:22,467
Come with us.

274
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,167
But you don't have to go in.

275
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:26,467
Just keep an eye outside.

276
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,667
Yes, sir.
I will get the cars ready.

277
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:30,567
- [DOOR OPENS]
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

278
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:37,633
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

279
00:12:37,767 --> 00:12:38,967
[EXHALES] Pa.

280
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:41,900
I failed to get back
at Mr. Chan.

281
00:12:42,033 --> 00:12:43,033
But I'll try again.

282
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,500
I've heard that before, Lucas.

283
00:12:47,233 --> 00:12:48,900
Don't be all talk.

284
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:50,100
Do it.

285
00:12:50,233 --> 00:12:51,433
Pa...

286
00:12:51,567 --> 00:12:53,100
give me another chance.

287
00:12:53,233 --> 00:12:54,200
[GLASS THUDS]

288
00:12:54,933 --> 00:12:56,833
In the world we live in,

289
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:01,700
not everyone
gets a second chance.

290
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:03,100
Sometimes, failing just once

291
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,000
means it's over for you.

292
00:13:05,133 --> 00:13:06,333
You're done.

293
00:13:06,467 --> 00:13:08,000
There's no way
to make up for it.

294
00:13:09,167 --> 00:13:13,433
Be grateful
you were born a Zafra.

295
00:13:15,567 --> 00:13:16,533
[DOOR OPENS]

296
00:13:16,667 --> 00:13:17,700
Pa...

297
00:13:18,433 --> 00:13:20,033
- I promise
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

298
00:13:20,167 --> 00:13:21,800
I won't fail you this time.

299
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,133
Prove it.

300
00:13:23,767 --> 00:13:25,333
That's enough.

301
00:13:25,467 --> 00:13:27,933
Mariano, let's go.

302
00:13:29,367 --> 00:13:30,533
[LUCAS SIGHS]

303
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,933
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

304
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:39,267
[DOOR OPENS]

305
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:42,867
- [DOOR CLOSES]
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

306
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,267
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

307
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:46,333
[DOOR OPENS]

308
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:49,233
Mr. Chan.

309
00:13:49,367 --> 00:13:51,833
[KEYS JANGLING]

310
00:13:51,967 --> 00:13:52,967
[GATE OPENS]

311
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,367
Where are you taking me?

312
00:13:56,500 --> 00:13:57,367
I'm free now?

313
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:58,267
No.

314
00:13:58,400 --> 00:13:59,867
We'll move you
to a new cell. Come.

315
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:00,800
Where?

316
00:14:00,933 --> 00:14:02,067
- There.
- Where?

317
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,567
Oh, no, no, no!

318
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:05,667
Come on. Just go.

319
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,667
- That's enough.
- No! No!

320
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,367
That's an order from the bosses.

321
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,400
No!

322
00:14:10,533 --> 00:14:11,400
Lock it.

323
00:14:11,533 --> 00:14:12,567
[GATE CREAKS]

324
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:14,967
[KEYS JANGLING]

325
00:14:16,633 --> 00:14:17,600
It's good.

326
00:14:17,733 --> 00:14:18,933
We're together now.

327
00:14:20,633 --> 00:14:21,600
No.

328
00:14:23,467 --> 00:14:24,633
It's too bad.

329
00:14:26,033 --> 00:14:28,833
Because only one of us
will come out of here alive.

330
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:39,267
[MUSIC TURNS GLUM]

331
00:14:42,933 --> 00:14:44,400
[VICTOR GRUNTS SOFTLY]

332
00:14:50,633 --> 00:14:51,867
[METAL RODS CLACKING]

333
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,167
[VICTOR]<i> Who are you?!
</i> What do you need from me?!

334
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,700
<i>A huge bounty's been placed
on your head</i>

335
00:14:55,833 --> 00:14:57,600
<i>for ruining the lives
of countless people.</i>

336
00:14:57,733 --> 00:14:59,200
<i>You deserve to rot
behind bars!</i>

337
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:00,567
<i> - Aah!
</i>- [BLOWS LANDING]

338
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:02,567
<i> Whoever you are, you bastard,</i>

339
00:15:02,733 --> 00:15:05,033
<i>you've no idea
who you're messing with.</i>

340
00:15:05,167 --> 00:15:08,700
<i>The moment I get out of here,
I'll hunt you down.</i>

341
00:15:08,833 --> 00:15:12,433
<i>I'll make you pay big time,
you fool.</i>

342
00:15:14,467 --> 00:15:15,700
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

343
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:18,633
[ISOBEL] Ricardo, everything is
ready for your gathering.

344
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,500
Well, I'm hoping one
of the guests

345
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:27,800
will help open doors
to potential investors.

346
00:15:28,067 --> 00:15:29,567
I'll invite Pinky

347
00:15:29,567 --> 00:15:33,100
so that she can help
encourage investors.

348
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:34,267
[RICARDO] Please do.

349
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:37,067
Isobel, there's only one thing
I want to happen today.

350
00:15:37,067 --> 00:15:40,133
For them to see my life
after retiring.

351
00:15:40,133 --> 00:15:42,533
That I'm still successful
despite having...

352
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:44,700
[INHALES DEEPLY]

353
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:47,967
having a daughter like Sam.

354
00:15:48,633 --> 00:15:49,700
[SIGHS]

355
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:53,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

356
00:15:53,533 --> 00:15:56,967
She's part
of your success, Ricardo.

357
00:15:59,933 --> 00:16:00,867
[HUFFS]

358
00:16:10,133 --> 00:16:12,300
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

359
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:14,800
- I think this needs replacing.
- Hey, Rudy.

360
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:17,133
What are you doing out here?
Go get some rest.

361
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:19,467
Staying at home
makes me feel weaker.

362
00:16:19,767 --> 00:16:22,200
Besides, I really want
to get back to work.

363
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:24,500
How could you not feel drained?

364
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:27,967
Betchay just won't stop
running her mouth.

365
00:16:27,967 --> 00:16:29,000
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

366
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,600
Hold on, let me change
the subject...

367
00:16:31,833 --> 00:16:34,500
Did you ever find out
who shot you?

368
00:16:35,633 --> 00:16:37,367
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

369
00:16:37,367 --> 00:16:40,300
Honestly, I can't think
of anybody.

370
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,533
All I can remember is...

371
00:16:43,533 --> 00:16:46,167
I was in the middle of a fight,
and then someone fired a gun.

372
00:16:46,167 --> 00:16:47,700
I have no idea who it was.

373
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,833
You know,
I think my hunch is right.

374
00:16:52,833 --> 00:16:55,767
Nobody else had a gun
except the police,

375
00:16:56,033 --> 00:16:58,033
so I believe they're the ones
who shot you.

376
00:16:58,533 --> 00:17:01,200
And remember that reporter?

377
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,600
- That... Salvador Manalo.
- Uh-- Yes, it's Salvador.

378
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:06,767
He witnessed everything
that day.

379
00:17:06,767 --> 00:17:12,500
I keep seeing his face on TV,
calling out the police.

380
00:17:12,767 --> 00:17:15,533
Yeah. That's why Betchay
was interviewed.

381
00:17:16,067 --> 00:17:18,133
To get the full story.

382
00:17:18,133 --> 00:17:22,133
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

383
00:17:22,133 --> 00:17:23,500
Finally.

384
00:17:23,867 --> 00:17:26,100
You kept your favorite agent
in check.

385
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:28,633
- I don't have favorites.
- Really?

386
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:30,600
[CHUCKLES DRYLY] That's funny.

387
00:17:30,600 --> 00:17:33,700
Because if another person had
done those repeated offenses,

388
00:17:34,300 --> 00:17:36,067
you would've sacked them
ages ago.

389
00:17:36,067 --> 00:17:39,400
Samantha made a mistake,

390
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,800
and she'll be held
accountable for it.

391
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:44,467
But a single mistake can't undo

392
00:17:44,467 --> 00:17:47,167
all the good she's brought
to the NCIA.

393
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:48,600
[PIA SCOFFS]

394
00:17:48,633 --> 00:17:50,733
- A single mistake?
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

395
00:17:50,733 --> 00:17:52,533
Illegal arrest.

396
00:17:52,533 --> 00:17:55,167
Unauthorized interrogation.

397
00:17:55,167 --> 00:17:57,433
Assault on a witness.

398
00:17:57,433 --> 00:18:00,167
Those are far
from simple mistakes, sir.

399
00:18:00,167 --> 00:18:02,900
That's why she was suspended.

400
00:18:02,900 --> 00:18:04,367
Yes, she's hard-headed.

401
00:18:04,367 --> 00:18:06,600
But her principles are
harder still.

402
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:07,933
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

403
00:18:07,933 --> 00:18:09,567
She will bounce back.

404
00:18:09,567 --> 00:18:11,033
She will learn from this.

405
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,467
Excuse me.

406
00:18:14,867 --> 00:18:18,833
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

407
00:18:18,833 --> 00:18:20,500
[HARRISS, STALLONE HUFFING]

408
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:22,500
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:18:22,533 --> 00:18:23,800
How's the training going?

410
00:18:24,033 --> 00:18:25,733
- Ongoing, boss.
- That's right, boss.

411
00:18:25,733 --> 00:18:26,833
- So, what's the plan?
- [MAN] Keep going.

412
00:18:26,833 --> 00:18:29,033
Is it time to strike
Samantha Jacinto?

413
00:18:29,033 --> 00:18:32,200
[LEE] Just tell us what
you want us to do with her.

414
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,967
We're ready anytime, boss.

415
00:18:34,233 --> 00:18:35,700
We'll get back at her for you.

416
00:18:35,967 --> 00:18:38,067
I'll take revenge for myself.

417
00:18:38,067 --> 00:18:40,500
What, you think I can't do it?

418
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:41,733
Boss, we didn't mean it
like that.

419
00:18:41,733 --> 00:18:42,933
Shut up!

420
00:18:43,467 --> 00:18:46,833
I have to prove to Papa that
I can carry out his orders.

421
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:49,533
I can't afford another failure.

422
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:51,467
I have to redeem myself.

423
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:53,367
But Mama's right.

424
00:18:53,367 --> 00:18:54,900
There's a proper time for this.

425
00:18:55,333 --> 00:18:57,933
We'll strike Samantha Jacinto...

426
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:00,200
when she least expects it.

427
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:03,267
[MUSIC SWELLING]

428
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,267
[MUSIC ENDS]

429
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:11,600
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

430
00:19:22,133 --> 00:19:23,233
De Luna!

431
00:19:23,233 --> 00:19:24,700
- Ma'am.
- Come here.

432
00:19:27,033 --> 00:19:28,733
Where is Sebastian?

433
00:19:29,267 --> 00:19:30,600
He stepped out, ma'am.

434
00:19:30,867 --> 00:19:33,500
Together with Ma'am Jacinto
and the whole team.

435
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,533
- Jacinto is with him?
- Yes, ma'am.

436
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:38,800
- Dismissed.
- Yes, ma'am.

437
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:43,100
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

438
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:44,333
[MUSIC FADES, ENDS]

439
00:19:44,667 --> 00:19:45,800
[DOOR OPENS]

440
00:19:47,933 --> 00:19:51,033
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

441
00:19:51,033 --> 00:19:52,100
[DOOR CLOSES]

442
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:55,567
We're here for your detainee,
Victor Zafra.

443
00:19:55,567 --> 00:19:56,767
I'm the lawyer.

444
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:58,600
They're the family.

445
00:19:58,600 --> 00:20:00,500
[POLICE OFFICER] You'll need
clearance to bring anyone else.

446
00:20:00,933 --> 00:20:03,600
We're not just anybody.

447
00:20:03,633 --> 00:20:04,600
Again,

448
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:07,433
we're the family
of Victor Zafra.

449
00:20:07,433 --> 00:20:10,533
[LAWYER] What we're doing
isn't against the protocol.

450
00:20:10,533 --> 00:20:12,267
- If we need clearance,
- [DOOR CLOSES]

451
00:20:12,267 --> 00:20:14,833
then let us speak
with Director Delgado.

452
00:20:14,833 --> 00:20:16,200
Understood. Just a moment.

453
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:19,467
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

454
00:20:19,467 --> 00:20:24,800
[MUSIC BECOMES TENSE]

455
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:25,767
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

456
00:20:25,767 --> 00:20:27,200
- Director.
- Yes?

457
00:20:28,633 --> 00:20:30,733
Victor Zafra's parents are
waiting downstairs

458
00:20:30,733 --> 00:20:31,967
with their lawyer.

459
00:20:32,867 --> 00:20:33,867
[DELGADO] Hmm.

460
00:20:34,067 --> 00:20:37,700
Are you saying
Col. Mariano Zafra is here?

461
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,133
Yes, sir. They're requesting
to see their son.

462
00:20:40,133 --> 00:20:46,833
I'm sure they came here
to get their criminal son out.

463
00:20:46,833 --> 00:20:48,867
- I'll deal with them.
- Yes, sir.

464
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:55,833
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

465
00:20:59,033 --> 00:21:00,167
Mrs. Zafra.

466
00:21:03,867 --> 00:21:04,933
Mariano.

467
00:21:04,933 --> 00:21:05,867
[MARIANO SCOFFS]

468
00:21:05,867 --> 00:21:07,167
Delgado!

469
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:10,333
You're still active
in the service?

470
00:21:10,333 --> 00:21:11,867
Yes, I'm still active.

471
00:21:11,867 --> 00:21:15,633
I'm still upholding the law
and standing for what's right.

472
00:21:15,633 --> 00:21:16,800
Not like you.

473
00:21:17,433 --> 00:21:19,733
All you have are allegations
against my son!

474
00:21:19,733 --> 00:21:21,700
It's no surprise that
you're Victor's father.

475
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:23,333
The apple doesn't fall far
from the tree.

476
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:25,033
You still haven't changed.

477
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:27,767
You're still driven
by your own interests.

478
00:21:27,767 --> 00:21:29,700
I haven't forgotten, Mariano,

479
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:33,667
how you ruined our operation
against the kidnapping ring!

480
00:21:34,133 --> 00:21:36,900
That was a failure
on the NCIA's part!

481
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:39,433
My reputation
at the NLEA is solid,

482
00:21:39,433 --> 00:21:42,467
from the day I entered service
until the day I retired!

483
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:45,367
Whatever you're planning
by coming here,

484
00:21:45,367 --> 00:21:47,700
I'll make sure
you won't succeed.

485
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:50,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

486
00:21:50,233 --> 00:21:53,600
We came here to talk to our son.

487
00:21:53,900 --> 00:21:55,000
Not you.

488
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:08,500
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- [SHAKER RATTLING]

489
00:22:08,633 --> 00:22:10,533
[WOMAN] Has someone
hit the jackpot yet?

490
00:22:10,667 --> 00:22:14,033
Letter B number three!

491
00:22:14,167 --> 00:22:16,333
- Has someone won yet?
- [SHAKER RATTLING]

492
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:23,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

493
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:27,133
Hello.

494
00:22:29,267 --> 00:22:30,467
Where's the money?

495
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:32,500
Boss Django...

496
00:22:32,633 --> 00:22:35,800
The money I got is just enough
for my husband's funeral.

497
00:22:39,567 --> 00:22:42,433
What's the point of
your husband's 3-month wake?

498
00:22:42,567 --> 00:22:43,800
How will you pay me back?!

499
00:22:43,933 --> 00:22:46,967
I just want to bury my husband.

500
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:48,833
Please,
let's put my father to rest.

501
00:22:49,467 --> 00:22:50,567
Put to rest?

502
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:52,667
- [YELPS]
- Put to rest?

503
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:54,667
Do you want me to do
the same to your kid?

504
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:57,800
No, boss. Please!

505
00:23:00,300 --> 00:23:01,800
You really don't have
the money?

506
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:03,867
Nothing?

507
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:07,400
[LAUGHS]

508
00:23:07,533 --> 00:23:08,767
Nothing at all?

509
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:13,967
- [OBJECTS CLATTERING]
- [SCREAMING]

510
00:23:14,967 --> 00:23:16,533
[MAN] Scram! All of you!

511
00:23:17,167 --> 00:23:18,367
C'mon, Gabo.

512
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:21,133
You even meddled
with those kids' problem.

513
00:23:21,267 --> 00:23:23,133
[BINOY] Those kids
were up to no good.

514
00:23:23,300 --> 00:23:25,900
It's because their parents
aren't around.

515
00:23:26,033 --> 00:23:27,433
That's the problem.

516
00:23:27,567 --> 00:23:30,033
Their parents should
be around to care for them.

517
00:23:30,167 --> 00:23:32,133
- You're right.
- To guide them.

518
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:34,933
You.

519
00:23:35,467 --> 00:23:36,633
Find a way to give
my money back.

520
00:23:36,767 --> 00:23:38,067
Do it now!

521
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:40,767
[WOMAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

522
00:23:40,900 --> 00:23:43,333
Pray that your mother
gets the money,

523
00:23:43,467 --> 00:23:44,767
or else you'll end up
like your father!

524
00:23:44,900 --> 00:23:46,133
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [MAN GRUNTS]

525
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:48,300
[MAN] Help!
Someone take a video!

526
00:23:48,433 --> 00:23:49,233
[TEKLA] Hey!

527
00:23:49,367 --> 00:23:52,033
Watch where you're going!

528
00:23:53,067 --> 00:23:55,633
[WOMAN] Gabo, please help me!

529
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:58,333
Django is causing trouble
at my husband's wake.

530
00:23:58,467 --> 00:24:00,433
I haven't been able to bury
my spouse for 3 months

531
00:24:00,567 --> 00:24:02,467
because he's claiming
all the money.

532
00:24:02,600 --> 00:24:04,767
Gabo, we need to go.

533
00:24:04,900 --> 00:24:07,267
- Why are we going there?
- We'll end up in trouble!

534
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:08,267
Pa...

535
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:11,400
Pray that your mother
gets me the money.

536
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:12,767
Or else,

537
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:14,900
you'll end up floating
in the river like your father!

538
00:24:15,033 --> 00:24:16,000
Do you understand?!

539
00:24:16,133 --> 00:24:17,200
[CRYING] Yes...

540
00:24:19,233 --> 00:24:20,067
Django!

541
00:24:20,200 --> 00:24:21,433
[TEKLA] Gabo,
let's just leave, please!

542
00:24:21,567 --> 00:24:25,400
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

543
00:24:25,533 --> 00:24:27,233
Gabo.

544
00:24:29,767 --> 00:24:31,000
What the hell are you doing?

545
00:24:33,300 --> 00:24:35,333
You really won't leave
the poor alone, won't you?

546
00:24:36,533 --> 00:24:37,933
They're already poor,

547
00:24:39,033 --> 00:24:40,333
and yet you're
still abusing them!

548
00:24:42,833 --> 00:24:44,300
What do you guys want?

549
00:24:44,433 --> 00:24:46,100
Do you want us to wipe
each other out here?!

550
00:24:46,233 --> 00:24:47,433
Go ahead!

551
00:24:47,567 --> 00:24:49,467
Until blood flows here in Tondo!

552
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:51,233
And only one group will be
left standing here!

553
00:24:51,367 --> 00:24:58,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

554
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:01,433
I'll count to three.

555
00:25:03,900 --> 00:25:05,067
Or I'll end you.

556
00:25:07,267 --> 00:25:08,433
One.

557
00:25:11,300 --> 00:25:12,367
Two.

558
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:19,467
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

559
00:25:21,467 --> 00:25:22,667
Three.

560
00:25:22,867 --> 00:25:25,033
<i>What happened to the NCIA?
Didn't they recognize you?</i>

561
00:25:25,167 --> 00:25:27,300
<i>They might be looking for you!
Don't drag us with you!</i>

562
00:25:27,433 --> 00:25:31,033
<i>We caught Mr. Chan,
but ended up in this situation.</i>

563
00:25:31,167 --> 00:25:34,467
<i>You need to work with us
if you want to live.</i>

564
00:25:34,600 --> 00:25:37,467
<i>Be our state witness
against Victor Zafra.</i>

565
00:25:37,633 --> 00:25:38,833
<i>You probably already
snitched to the NCIA!</i>

566
00:25:38,967 --> 00:25:40,567
[GRUNTS]

567
00:25:40,700 --> 00:25:42,667
<i>We need to get Victor
out of there!</i>

568
00:25:42,800 --> 00:25:46,233
<i>If we need to storm the NCIA
to break him out,</i>

569
00:25:46,367 --> 00:25:48,733
<i>- I'll do it, Ma!
- Will you fight back?</i>

570
00:25:48,867 --> 00:25:52,167
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

571
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:54,167
<i>We're the NCIA!
What if we finish you all off?!</i>

572
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:56,967
<i>If they file a complaint
against us,</i>

573
00:25:57,100 --> 00:25:58,567
<i> we might end up suspended!</i>

574
00:25:58,700 --> 00:26:00,167
<i>We might be able
to catch up to them!</i>

575
00:26:00,300 --> 00:26:02,667
<i>- Gabo! Help!
- Help us, Gabo!</i>
